    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. the tables help a lot. i'm mostly concerned about the quality of the wood itself, though. since it's Douglas fir, i'm worried about getting a beam that looks okay on the outside but has some hidden knots or internal splits that could mess with the load capacity. how do i actually check for those kinds of internal issues that aren't immediately obvious just by looking at the surface?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
